{# One tier per render; the caller loops over the tiers it has. Byte-
   deterministic for equal inputs, so no timestamps and no guidance fence.
   `readonly` is a subagent without file tools: it reads the index but
   can neither open the detail files it points to nor write one, so the
   write instruction is dropped and the pointers are named as text.
   `subagent` reads memory and never writes it, so it gets no write
   instruction either. #}
<memory path="{{ path }}">
{% if content %}
{{ content }}
{% if readonly %}
Read-only here: this run has no filesystem, so the files these lines point to cannot be opened. Use the lines themselves.
{% endif %}
{% elif readonly or subagent | default(false) %}
No {{ path }} exists yet.
{% else %}
No {{ path }} exists yet. When you learn something durable, create a typed detail file with frontmatter and add a one-line pointer to it here. Keep {{ path }} an index, not a memory.
{% endif %}
</memory>
